# Compact dictionary copy; process detail stays in the system and courses.
DEFINITION_TEXT = {
'source':'The origin of an opportunity, supported by the credited sourcing user, campaign or partner. It stays separate from the current owner and transaction route.',
'conversion':'The progression from Contact qualification to opportunity creation and sales qualification. MQL and AQL are separate entry paths; SAL is recorded at creation and SQL on first entry to Discovery.',
'sal-review':'The assigned seller’s decision to accept or reject an opportunity handoff. This decision is separate from the SAL milestone recorded at opportunity creation.',
'challenge':'The customer’s initial problem or unmet need, supported by customer evidence.',
'authority':'The contact’s role and influence in the buying decision, including access to those who approve the purchase.',
'money':'Evidence of the customer’s funding, funding access and ability to pay for the project.',
'priority':'The urgency and business importance of solving the customer’s problem, including the consequence of delay.',
'stack':'The customer’s current technical environment, workloads and relevant storage requirements.',
'use-case':'The activity or workflow the customer intends to support with the solution, and the outcome they want to achieve.',
'route':'How the sale will transact: Direct or Indirect. Indirect requires an applicable Indirect Route Type.',
'pain':'The customer’s problem and its validated impact on people, operations or business results. It develops the initial CHAMPS Challenge into a clear reason to act.',
'competition':'The alternatives the customer is considering, including other vendors and keeping the current approach.',
'technical-value':'How the proposed solution meets the customer’s technical requirements, including the configuration and evidence supporting its fit.',
'champion':'An internal customer advocate whose influence and support are demonstrated through actions that help the opportunity progress.',
'criteria':'The requirements the customer uses to evaluate and compare solutions.',
'technical-outcome':'The result of technical evaluation: Technical Win or Technical Loss. Technical Win is required before Stage 4.',
'operational-value':'The measurable improvement the solution is expected to deliver to the customer’s operations, expressed as a baseline, target and measurement approach.',
'economic-buyer':'The person who controls the budget for the purchase.',
'decision-process':'The steps, participants and timing through which the customer selects a solution.',
'business-value':'The quantified economic justification for the purchase, based on customer-validated benefits, costs and assumptions.',
'paper-process':'The legal, procurement, signature and purchase-order steps required to complete the transaction.',
'procurement':'The documents and confirmations needed to complete procurement, including the PO, final agreements, IPG disposition and applicable delivery information.',
'won-decision':'The customer’s decision to buy, recorded before Order Management confirms the booked order. The sales forecast remains Commit.',
'booking':'Order Management’s confirmation that the order is reconciled and booked. It establishes Closed won and locks booked facts and Close Date.',
'invoice':'Completion of the Opportunity at Stage 8 when the full in-scope order is verified as delivered on site. Financial invoicing, deployment and value assessment are separate events.',
'loss':'An assessment of why the customer did not buy, what the team learned and what follow-up is appropriate.',
'quoting':'The creation and revision of commercial proposals in CPQ, permitted during Stages 2–5.',
'next-steps':'The weekly confirmation of the next customer action and expected Close Date for open opportunities in Stages 1–6. The SE reviews its technical action separately.',
'buying-committee':'The people involved in evaluating, influencing, funding and approving the purchase, linked as Salesforce Contacts with their opportunity roles.',
'poc':'A proof of concept: a scoped evaluation used to test technical requirements. A required POC must be Cancelled or Completed before Stage 3; completion alone does not establish a Technical Win.',
'risk':'A technical issue or uncertainty that could affect the opportunity, recorded with its category, severity, explanation and linked issue.',
'enhancements':'Requests for needed product capabilities, documented in Cases linked to the opportunity. A request is not a delivery commitment.',
'partner-accounts':'The organizations involved in an opportunity, with their roles, impact, contacts and engagement plans.',
'fulfillment':'The partner account responsible for fulfillment. It may differ from the sourcing partner and the actual ship-to destination.',
'partner-credit':'The classification of partner involvement based on channel ownership at creation and the earliest qualifying partner event. Automated credit freezes at booking.',
'nvidia':'NVIDIA’s involvement in an opportunity, recorded through its account-specific engagement plan and the Opportunity’s engagement summary and status.',
'logistics':'Planning that connects shipping, customer receipt and installation, including the dates, responsibilities and dependencies for each.',
'ipg':'The process for gathering, finalizing and submitting the IPG package during procurement and carrying it into the order and deployment handoff.',
'win-wire':'A manager-reviewed summary of why a deal was won, the customer value and the contributors. Above $1M, it is submitted to Enablement / #win-wire within two business days.',
'interviews':'Whether the Win/Loss team may approach a customer for feedback. Yes requires a Salesforce Contact; No requires a reason the team cannot approach.',
'deployment':'The Case that coordinates deployment scope, ownership, plans and workstreams, starting at Won decision and continuing after the Opportunity ends.',
'value-realization':'Confirmation that the customer achieved the agreed operational and business outcomes, supported by measured results and customer evidence.',
'time-to-value':'The number of days from first verified on-site delivery to confirmed value achievement. It is calculated on the coordinating Case only when Value Achieved? is Yes.',
'forecast':'The sales forecast classification derived from the Opportunity stage: Pre-pipeline, Pipeline, Upside, Commit, Won or Loss.',
'deal-context':'The customer, solution and business-need summary, supported by links to current technical documentation.',
 'term-sal-sales-accepted-lead':'The conversion milestone recorded when an opportunity is created. Despite its name, SAL does not itself confirm the assigned seller’s acceptance; that is a separate decision.',
 'term-value-achieved':'The Case’s value-assessment outcome: Yes means achieved and confirmed; No means assessed and not achieved; blank means the assessment is pending.',
 'term-nvidia-engagement-status':'The Opportunity-level status describing NVIDIA’s engagement when its association is active. The exact field and allowed choices remain to be confirmed; association Active/Inactive is a separate status.',
 'term-seller-self-qualified-entry':'Direct creation of a seller-qualified opportunity in Stage 1 by its assigned seller, recording auto-accepted SAL and SQL. CHAMPS is completed before Stage 2.',
 'stage-creation':'The capture of a new opportunity, its source, originating Contact and core deal information. Inbound intake starts in Validate; seller-self-qualified opportunities may start in Discovery.',
 'stage-s0':'The stage for reviewing an inbound handoff, assigning the seller and completing acceptance and CHAMPS qualification before Discovery.',
 'stage-s1':'The stage for establishing business fit, use case, buying roles and route to market. Entry records SQL; discovery is completed before Solution design.',
 'stage-s2':'The stage for evaluating technical fit through candidate configurations, supported by pain, criteria, competitor and champion evidence.',
 'stage-s3':'The stage for agreeing one configuration and aligning the technical outcome, operational value, Economic Buyer and Decision Process.',
 'stage-s4':'The stage for aligning the commercial proposal, quantified Business Value, Primary Quote and Paper Process.',
 'stage-s5':'The stage for completing the PO, final agreements, IPG disposition and applicable shipping and delivery information.',
 'stage-s6':'The customer’s won decision, followed by order review and deployment planning. The opportunity remains Commit until booking is confirmed.',
 'stage-s7':'The OM-confirmed booked order, with locked booked facts and Close Date. Fulfillment and deployment coordination continue.',
 'stage-s8':'The final Opportunity stage, reached at verified delivery of the complete in-scope order. Invoice evidence is captured when issued; deployment and value work continue on the Case.',
 'stage-lost':'The outcome recording the customer’s decision not to buy, with the reason, competitive outcome, learning and follow-up.',
 'stage-post':'The delivery and validation of the customer’s agreed outcome, managed on the coordinating Case. It continues after Stage 8 rather than adding an Opportunity stage.'
}

